{"parse": {"title": "Fishing spot (aerial fishing)", "pageid": 276797, "revid": 15314053, "redirects": [], "wikitext": {"*": "{{obsolete|The chance of receiving Molch pearls were increased in the [[19 August]] [[2026]] [[Update:Summer Sweep Up - Hunter & Skilling|game update]].}}\n{{otheruses|def=no|the activity where these spots are fished from|aerial fishing|the spot that will automatically catch multiple fish|frenzied fishing spot}}{{Infobox NPC\n|name = Fishing spot\n|image = [[File:Fishing spot (aerial fishing).png|300px]]\n|release = [[10 January]] [[2019]]\n|update = The Kebos Lowlands\n|members = Yes\n|location = [[Lake Molch]]\n|options = Catch\n|examine = I can see fish swimming in the water.\n|map = No\n|id = 8523\n|leagueRegion = Kourend\n}}\n'''Fishing spots''' can be found on the island in [[Lake Molch]]. These spots are used to catch [[Bluegill]], [[Common tench]], [[Mottled eel]], [[Greater siren]] and a [[Golden tench]].\n\n==Location==\n{{ObjectTableHead}}\n{{ObjectLocLine\n|name = Fishing spot (aerial fishing)\n|location = [[Lake Molch]]\n|members = Yes\n|mapID = 0\n|plane = 0\n|x:1382,y:3627|x:1354,y:3640|x:1380,y:3631|x:1353,y:3630|x:1380,y:3627|x:1354,y:3634|x:1353,y:3628|x:1353,y:3631|x:1355,y:3638|x:1371,y:3624|x:1380,y:3632|x:1382,y:3626|x:1382,y:3633|x:1379,y:3628|x:1379,y:3634|x:1381,y:3631|x:1379,y:3622|x:1358,y:3639|x:1357,y:3629|x:1379,y:3627\n|mtype = pin\n|leagueRegion = kourend\n}}\n{{ObjectTableBottom}}\n\n==Fishing info==\n{{Fishing info\n|name = Fishing spot\n|level = 43\n|skill2name = Hunter\n|skill2lvl = 35\n|skill1exp = Varies\n|skill2exp = Varies\n|tool = {{plink|Cormorant's glove}}\n|bait = {{plink|King worm}} or {{plink|Fish offcuts}}\n|bucket = No\n}}\n\n===Fish===\n{{DropsTableHead}}\n{{DropsLineSkill|name=Bluegill|quantity=1|rarity=varies|skill=Fishing|level=43}}\n{{DropsLineSkill|name=Common tench|quantity=1|rarity=varies|skill=Fishing|level=56}}\n{{DropsLineSkill|name=Mottled eel|quantity=1|rarity=varies|skill=Fishing|level=73}}\n{{DropsLineSkill|name=Greater siren|quantity=1|rarity=varies|skill=Fishing|level=91}}\n{{DropsLineSkill|name=Golden tench|quantity=1|rarity=very rare (1/20,000)|skill=Fishing|level=43}}\n{{DropsTableBottom}}\n\n===Secondary===\n{{DropsTableHead}}\n{{DropsLineSkill|name=Clue bottle (beginner)|quantity=1|rarity=Rare|skill=Fishing}}\n{{DropsLineSkill|name=Clue bottle (easy)|quantity=1|rarity=Rare|skill=Fishing}}\n{{DropsLineSkill|name=Clue bottle (medium)|quantity=1|rarity=Rare|skill=Fishing}}\n{{DropsLineSkill|name=Clue bottle (hard)|quantity=1|rarity=Rare|skill=Fishing}}\n{{DropsLineSkill|name=Clue bottle (elite)|quantity=1|rarity=Rare|skill=Fishing}}\n{{DropsLineSkill|name=Molch pearl|quantity=1|rarity=1.5/100|altrarity=1/50|altraritydash=-|raritynotes=<ref group=\"d\">[[Aerial fishing#Molch pearls|Between 1/66.67 and 1/50 chance]] depending on [[Fishing]] and [[Hunter]] levels{{Citation needed}}.</ref>|skill=Fishing}}\n{{DropsTableBottom}}\n\n===Catch formula===\nThe formula for what type of fish is caught is as follows.\n\nPick a random number 0 to (X-1) inclusive, where <math>X= \\frac {Fishing \\ level \\times 2 + Hunter \\ level}{3}</math>\n*If the number is 82+, the player will receive a [[greater siren]] if the player meets the level requirements.\n*If it's 67+, the player will receive a [[mottled eel]] if the player meets the level requirements.\n*If it's 52+, the player will receive a [[common tench]] if the player meets the level requirements.\n*Any other number and the player will receive a [[bluegill]].{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1139091986865111041|date=13 June 2019|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/100795|archivedate=13 June 2019|quote=Define X = (((Fishing level x 2) + Hunter level) / 3). Pick a random number 0 to (X-1) inclusive. If it's 82+ it'll give a siren if you have the stats. If it's 67+ it'll give an eel if you have the stats. If it's 52+ it'll give a tench if you have the stats. Else bluegill.}}\n*However it should be remembered that just because you have a required level, it does not mean you will only catch that kind of fish. Just meeting the requirements to catch a fish may not give you a high enough roll to actually catch the given fish, and small values above the requirements give a very small chance. You can use the [[Calculator:Fishing/Aerial fishing|Aerial fishing calculator]] to estimate the catch rate at a given Hunter and Fishing level.\n\n==References==\n{{Reflist}}\n\n{{Lake Molch}}\n{{Fishing spots}}\n{{Hunter}}"}}, "fetchedAt": "2026-10-06T04:22:11.027495+00:00", "dropHtml": "<table class=\"wikitable sortable filterable item-drops autosort=4,a\" style=\"text-align:center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th style=\"border-right: none;\" class=\"drops-img-header drop-disp-btn unsortable\" title=\"Sort items by category, rarity and name.\"></th>\n<th style=\"border-left: none;\" class=\"item-col\">Item</th>\n<th data-sort-type=\"number\">Quantity</th>\n<th>Rarity</th>\n<th class=\"ge-column\" data-sort-type=\"number\">Price</th>\n<th class=\"alch-column\" data-sort-type=\"number\">High Alch</th>\n</tr>\n\n<tr style=\"text-align:center\"><td class=\"inventory-image\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/w/Bluegill\" title=\"Bluegill\"><img alt=\"Bluegill.png: Fishing spot (aerial fishing) drops Bluegill with rarity Varies in quantity 1\" src=\"/images/Bluegill.png?04bdb\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"30\" height=\"22\" class=\"mw-file-element\" data-file-width=\"30\" data-file-height=\"22\" /></a></span></td><td class=\"item-col\" style=\"text-align:left\"><a href=\"/w/Bluegill\" title=\"Bluegill\">Bluegill</a></td><td data-sort-value=\"1\">1</td><td data-sort-value=\"4096\" class=\"table-bg-pink\"><span>Varies</span></td><td data-sort-value=\"48\" class=\"ge-column\" title=\"48 coins\" style=\"text-align:right;cursor:help\">48</td><td data-sort-value=\"1\" class=\"alch-column\" title=\"1 coin\" style=\"text